# Support

This guide explains how buyers can receive support for products purchased on the Codexeron Marketplace.

Codexeron aims to provide a reliable support experience for both buyers and sellers.

---

# Support Overview

Support may involve:

- Product questions
- Installation assistance
- Technical issues
- Account problems
- Payment questions
- License issues

---

# Types of Support

Support requests may be handled by:

## Seller Support

Product-specific questions are usually handled by the seller.

Examples:

- Product installation
- Configuration questions
- Feature explanations
- Product-related issues

---

## Codexeron Support

Codexeron support handles platform-related issues.

Examples:

- Account problems
- Payment issues
- Order problems
- License system issues
- Marketplace questions

---

# Before Contacting Support

Before requesting help:

- Read the product documentation.
- Check installation requirements.
- Review known issues.
- Verify your account and purchase information.

Providing detailed information helps resolve issues faster.

---

# Creating a Support Request

A useful support request should include:

- Product name
- Order information
- Problem description
- Error messages
- Screenshots when necessary
- Steps to reproduce the issue

---

# Support Communication

When requesting support:

- Be clear and respectful.
- Provide accurate information.
- Avoid sharing sensitive account information publicly.
- Follow support instructions carefully.

---

# Response Times

Response times may vary depending on:

- Support availability
- Issue complexity
- Seller activity
- Request volume

---

# Common Issues

Before contacting support, check:

- Product compatibility.
- Required server settings.
- Installation instructions.
- Product documentation.
- Latest available updates.

---

# Security

Never share:

- Passwords
- Private keys
- Payment credentials
- Sensitive personal information

Support teams will never request confidential credentials.

